 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Sounds like the chain needs little adjustment. Pulling at the sides usually does it without any tools. Of course. Turn it so the chain runs over the small gear at the bottom right and the big gear at the front. Then adjust it so the chain doesn't jump. Then the chain itself needs replacing. You can do it yourself or take it into a bike shop. How it rides is personal preference. Some people like a smooth, one speed bike. Others like the thrill of shifting.",
